</div>
<div id="S2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi=\pi_{1}\cdots\pi_{n}\in\mathfrak{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi=\pi_{1}\cdots\pi_{n}\in\mathfrak{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, and suppose that
<math id="S2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;i_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;i_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> determine a classical occurrence of <math id="S2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;v_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;v_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> be the selected values <math id="S2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{i_{1}},\ldots,\pi_{i_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{i_{1}},\ldots,\pi_{i_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> written in increasing
order, and set <math id="S2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{0}=v_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{0}=v_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{k+1}=v_{k+1}=n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{k+1}=v_{k+1}=n+1</annotation></semantics></math>. The selected entries form an <em id="S2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">occurrence</em> of the mesh pattern
<math id="S2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=(\tau,R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=(\tau,R)</annotation></semantics></math> if, for every <math id="S2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,b)\in R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,b)\in R</annotation></semantics></math>, there is no plot point
<math id="S2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j,\pi_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j,\pi_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="S2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{a}&lt;j&lt;i_{a+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{a}&lt;j&lt;i_{a+1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{b}&lt;\pi_{j}&lt;v_{b+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{b}&lt;\pi_{j}&lt;v_{b+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus each shaded square prescribes a rectangular region that must contain
no other point of the plot of <math id="S2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="S2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math>, this definition
reduces to classical pattern containment.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The <em id="S2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">boxed pattern</em> with underlying permutation <math id="S2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in\mathfrak{S}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in\mathfrak{S}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>
is <math id="S2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Box}(\tau)=\bigl(\tau,\{1,\ldots,k-1\}^{2}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Box</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Box}(\tau)=\bigl(\tau,\{1,\ldots,k-1\}^{2}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>. It is also denoted by a box drawn around the permutation, such as
<math id="S2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\mathstrut 123}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn>123</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\mathstrut 123}</annotation></semantics></math>, or by displaying its mesh:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Box}(123)=\boxed{\mathstrut 123}=\raisebox{2.58334pt}{\hbox to21.01pt{\vbox to21.01pt{\pgfpicture\makeatletter\hbox{\hskip 0.14825pt\lower-0.14825pt\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke=#000000} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill=#000000} \lxSVG@setlinewidth{\the\pgflinewidth}\lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke-width=0.4pt} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\nullfont\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} {{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}}{{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}}
{}{{}}{}
