<p id="S8.Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">be the border mesh pattern studied in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>. If <math id="S8.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{n,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{n,k}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes
the number of permutations in <math id="S8.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> with exactly <math id="S8.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> occurrences of
<math id="S8.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, then <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, Theorems 2 and 3]</cite>, for <math id="S8.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S8.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{n,k}=(n-2)!\bigl(H_{n-2}-H_{k}\bigr)\qquad(1\leq k\leq n-3)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{n,k}=(n-2)!\bigl(H_{n-2}-H_{k}\bigr)\qquad(1\leq k\leq n-3),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.Thmtheorem6.p1.3" class="ltx_p">whereas <math id="S8.Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{n,0}=(n-2)!\bigl(H_{n-2}+n^{2}-2n+2\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{n,0}=(n-2)!\bigl(H_{n-2}+n^{2}-2n+2\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Equation (<a href="#S8.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ Corollary 8.3. ‣ 8 Boxed 12 and strong Bruhat covers ‣ Coincidences and Growth of Boxed Mesh Patterns" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) is also the <math id="S8.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math> case of
Proposition <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem4" title="Proposition 6.4. ‣ 6.3 Average occurrence counts for boxed patterns ‣ 6 The boxed mesh pattern 123 ‣ Coincidences and Growth of Boxed Mesh Patterns" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.4</span></a>. The following direct derivation refines it by
the positional span of an occurrence. Fix positions <math id="S8.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;j</annotation></semantics></math> and put
<math id="S8.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=j-i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=j-i</annotation></semantics></math>. In the block <math id="S8.p7.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{i}\cdots\pi_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{i}\cdots\pi_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> the two endpoint ranks are a
uniformly distributed ordered pair of distinct elements of <math id="S8.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[d+1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[d+1]</annotation></semantics></math>. They
form a boxed <math id="S8.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>12</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12</annotation></semantics></math> occurrence exactly when the right endpoint has rank one
larger than the left endpoint. There are <math id="S8.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> such pairs out of <math id="S8.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(d+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(d+1)</annotation></semantics></math>, so</p>
<table id="S8.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\bigl((i,j)\text{ is a }\operatorname{Box}(12)\text{-occurrence}\bigr)=\frac{1}{d+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is a </mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Box</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>12</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-occurrence</mtext></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\bigl((i,j)\text{ is a }\operatorname{Box}(12)\text{-occurrence}\bigr)=\frac{1}{d+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p7.2" class="ltx_p">Linearity of expectation gives</p>
<table id="S8.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[b(\pi)]=\sum_{d=1}^{n-1}\frac{n-d}{d+1}=(n+1)H_{n}-2n." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[b(\pi)]=\sum_{d=1}^{n-1}\frac{n-d}{d+1}=(n+1)H_{n}-2n.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p7.3" class="ltx_p">Equivalently, the exponential generating function for the total number of
occurrences is</p>
<table id="S8.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n\geq 0}\frac{D_{n}^{\prime}(1)}{n!}x^{n}=\frac{-\log(1-x)-x}{(1-x)^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n\geq 0}\frac{D_{n}^{\prime}(1)}{n!}x^{n}=\frac{-\log(1-x)-x}{(1-x)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S8.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Maximum insertion gives an exact identity for the full distribution, although
it does not close in the single sequence of polynomials <math id="S8.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}(q)</annotation></semantics></math>. For a word
<math id="S8.p8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w=w_{1}\cdots w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=w_{1}\cdots w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with distinct entries, let <math id="S8.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{rlmax}(w)=|\{i\in[t]:w_{i}&gt;w_{j}\text{ for every }i&lt;j\leq t\}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>rlmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for every </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{rlmax}(w)=|\{i\in[t]:w_{i}&gt;w_{j}\text{ for every }i&lt;j\leq t\}|</annotation></semantics></math> be its number of right-to-left maxima, and set
<math id="S8.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{rlmax}(\varepsilon)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>rlmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{rlmax}(\varepsilon)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 8.7</span></span><span id="S8.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S8.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\mathfrak{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\mathfrak{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq t\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq t\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S8.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{(t)}=\pi_{1}\cdots\pi_{t}\,(n+1)\,\pi_{t+1}\cdots\pi_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t)}=\pi_{1}\cdots\pi_{t}\,(n+1)\,\pi_{t+1}\cdots\pi_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S8.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="b(\pi^{(t)})=b(\pi)+\operatorname{rlmax}(\pi_{1}\cdots\pi_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>rlmax</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(\pi^{(t)})=b(\pi)+\operatorname{rlmax}(\pi_{1}\cdots\pi_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="S8.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{n+1}(q)=\sum_{\pi\in\mathfrak{S}_{n}}q^{b(\pi)}\sum_{t=0}^{n}q^{\operatorname{rlmax}(\pi_{1}\cdots\pi_{t})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>rlmax</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n+1}(q)=\sum_{\pi\in\mathfrak{S}_{n}}q^{b(\pi)}\sum_{t=0}^{n}q^{\operatorname{rlmax}(\pi_{1}\cdots\pi_{t})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S8.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Inserting the new maximum neither creates nor destroys an occurrence using
only old entries. A new occurrence must end at <math id="S8.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Its first entry
<math id="S8.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S8.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leq t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leq t</annotation></semantics></math>, forms a boxed <math id="S8.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>12</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12</annotation></semantics></math> occurrence with <math id="S8.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n+1</annotation></semantics></math> exactly
when no later entry of the prefix <math id="S8.p9.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{1}\cdots\pi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}\cdots\pi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is larger than <math id="S8.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,
that is, exactly when <math id="S8.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a right-to-left maximum of the prefix. This
proves (<a href="#S8.E30" title="Equation 30 ‣ Proposition 8.7. ‣ 8 Boxed 12 and strong Bruhat covers ‣ Coincidences and Growth of Boxed Mesh Patterns" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>); summing over the <math id="S8.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n+1</annotation></semantics></math> insertion sites and
all parents proves (<a href="#S8.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ Proposition 8.7. ‣ 8 Boxed 12 and strong Bruhat covers ‣ Coincidences and Growth of Boxed Mesh Patterns" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Formula (<a href="#S8.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ Proposition 8.7. ‣ 8 Boxed 12 and strong Bruhat covers ‣ Coincidences and Growth of Boxed Mesh Patterns" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>) shows both the promise and the
difficulty of maximum insertion: a closed recurrence must retain the joint
distribution of <math id="S8.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> with the right-to-left-maximum counts of all
prefixes. We do not know a finite catalytic refinement that accomplishes
this, and the full polynomial <math id="S8.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}(q)</annotation></semantics></math> remains open.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">9 </span>Concluding directions</h2>

<div id="S9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The growth classification is complete except for one length-four orbit.
Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4.4. ‣ 4 The exceptional length-four patterns ‣ Coincidences and Growth of Boxed Mesh Patterns" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>, together with the factorial construction of
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>, shows that no boxed pattern of length at least five has the
Stanley–Wilf property. In length four, twenty patterns have factorial lower
bounds, the orbit <math id="S9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{2413,3142\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>2413</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3142</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{2413,3142\}</annotation></semantics></math> has semi-Baxter and hence exponential
growth, and only <math id="S9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{2143,3412\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>2143</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3412</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{2143,3412\}</annotation></semantics></math> remains unresolved. We conjecture that this orbit has factorial
growth; see Conjecture <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem5" title="Conjecture 7.5. ‣ 7 The remaining orbit {2143,3412} ‣ Coincidences and Growth of Boxed Mesh Patterns" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The coincidence results also reveal a sharp length boundary.
Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2. ‣ 5 Classical, vincular and bivincular coincidences ‣ Coincidences and Growth of Boxed Mesh Patterns" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a> shows that boxed–vincular
coincidences stop in length four, while Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 5.4. ‣ 5 Classical, vincular and bivincular coincidences ‣ Coincidences and Growth of Boxed Mesh Patterns" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>
shows that the genuinely bivincular coincidence in
Corollary <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Corollary 5.3. ‣ 5 Classical, vincular and bivincular coincidences ‣ Coincidences and Growth of Boxed Mesh Patterns" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a> is also maximal in length. The
interval-consecutive criterion provides a complementary structural viewpoint:
boxed <math id="S9.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> avoidance is consecutive <math id="S9.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> avoidance on every interval of
values. Moreover, Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Proposition 3.4. ‣ 3 Boxed patterns as interval-consecutive patterns ‣ Coincidences and Growth of Boxed Mesh Patterns" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a> transfers factorial
lower bounds from interval factors to larger boxed patterns.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For boxed <math id="S9.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="123" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>123</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">123</annotation></semantics></math>, Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 6.1. ‣ 6.1 Exact enumeration ‣ 6 The boxed mesh pattern 123 ‣ Coincidences and Growth of Boxed Mesh Patterns" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a> gives an exact maximum-insertion
identity and five new terms, while Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 6.2. ‣ 6.2 A subfactorial upper bound ‣ 6 The boxed mesh pattern 123 ‣ Coincidences and Growth of Boxed Mesh Patterns" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a> bounds its
growth exponent by a constant below <math id="S9.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.85" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.85</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.85</annotation></semantics></math>. A closed enumeration remains
open. Proposition <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem4" title="Proposition 6.4. ‣ 6.3 Average occurrence counts for boxed patterns ‣ 6 The boxed mesh pattern 123 ‣ Coincidences and Growth of Boxed Mesh Patterns" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.4</span></a> also shows that all boxed
patterns of a fixed length have the same first moment; in particular, the
expected number of boxed <math id="S9.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="123" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>123</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">123</annotation></semantics></math> occurrences is asymptotic to <math id="S9.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\log n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, for boxed <math id="S9.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>12</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12</annotation></semantics></math>, Proposition <a href="#S8.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 8.1. ‣ 8 Boxed 12 and strong Bruhat covers ‣ Coincidences and Growth of Boxed Mesh Patterns" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.1</span></a> identifies the occurrence
statistic with up-degree in the strong Bruhat order. Although
real-rootedness, <math id="S9.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-positivity and log-concavity fail in small lengths,
the available data motivate Conjecture <a href="#S8.Thmtheorem5" title="Conjecture 8.5. ‣ 8 Boxed 12 and strong Bruhat covers ‣ Coincidences and Growth of Boxed Mesh Patterns" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.5</span></a>, which asserts
unimodality of the distribution polynomials.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Declaration of generative AI and AI-assisted technologies in the
manuscript preparation process</h2>

<div id="Sx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">During the preparation of this work the authors used
GPT (OpenAI) in order to assist with language editing, exploratory testing of
conjectures, proof development, and the drafting of parts of the paper. After using this tool, the authors reviewed, corrected, and verified the
resulting text, arguments, and references, and take full responsibility for
the content of the manuscript.</p>
</div>
</section>
